course: dictionary
lesson: 5777
title: Lush: green, rich or lovely
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Lush» has more than one meaning, so the words around it tell you which one is right. In «a lush rainforest» or «lush grass», lush means green, thick and growing well. Look at the clues: rainforest and grass are about plants.
explain: In «lush velvet curtains», lush means rich and expensive-looking. Velvet is a soft, costly cloth, so the clue is in the word velvet. Check your meaning by swapping it in: if «rich velvet curtains» still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
explain: In UK slang, especially in Wales and the South West, «That cake was lush!» means lovely or delicious. Slang like this is informal, so say it with friends, not in a school essay. Lush also has a rude US meaning, a person who drinks too much alcohol, which is unkind, so never use it about people.
fact: Lush means green, thick and growing well when it describes plants or places, such as «lush grass» and «a lush rainforest».
fact: Lush can also mean rich and expensive-looking, as in «lush velvet curtains».
fact: In UK slang, especially in Wales and the South West, «lush» means lovely, great or delicious, as in «That cake was lush!»
fact: In informal US talk, a lush is a person who drinks too much alcohol. This is rude, so do not use it about people.
fact: To find the meaning, look for clues: rain and plants point to green, velvet points to rich, and cake points to delicious.
exercise: What does lush mean in «a lush rainforest»? | *Green, thick and growing well | Rich and expensive | Very dry and dusty | Lovely and delicious
exercise: In «lush velvet curtains», what does lush suggest? | Wet and muddy | Very small and plain | Lovely and delicious, like a cake | *Rich and expensive-looking
exercise: Chloe says, «that colour's lush». What does she probably mean? | Dark and gloomy | A person who drinks too much | *Lovely | Green and growing
test: «That cake was lush!» In this sentence, which meaning of lush fits? | Green and thick | Rich and expensive | *Lovely or delicious | A person who drinks too much
test: Which meaning of lush is rude, and should not be used about people? | Lovely or great | Rich and expensive | *A person who drinks too much alcohol | Green and growing
exam: Which word in «a lush rainforest» gives the best clue that lush means green and growing? | lush | *rainforest | the | a
ghost
